  "assertions": [
    "T3: the fingerprint computed on first delivery is written to Communications column R (ingress_fingerprint) and is non-empty when read back.",
    "T6: the resolver reads the stored fingerprint off the sheet on the next round and returns ALREADY_RECORDED for a byte-identical replay.",
    "T7a: an identical replay changes none of communication_id, subject, summary, classification, received_at, ingress_fingerprint.",
    "T7b: an identical replay adds no Communications row, adds no Actions row, and does not change Matters.updated_at.",
    "T9a: a changed-body replay returns IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT with requires_human_review true.",
    "T9b: a changed-body replay mutates nothing in Communications, Actions or Matters.",
    "T10: communication_id is identical across R1, R2, R3, the stored row, and the owner-facing Telegram notice text.",
    "Event ids are deterministic and distinct per outcome, so the three audit rows coexist instead of overwriting one another.",
